+## Routes added with sales
+
+- `POST /import/sales` takes `{ "csv": "ticket,soldAt,dishId,qty\n..." }` and
+  answers `{ "tickets", "dishes" }` (tickets imported; dishes = sum of `qty`).
+  Each dish uses one recipe portion per `qty` (ledger `ref` `sale:<ticket>`,
+  movement time = `soldAt`). Tickets already imported are skipped. A bad row
+  or a shortage imports nothing; the `bad_request` message names the row
+  (`row 2` is the first data row).
+- `GET /reports/variance?from=&to=` lists per item `theoretical` (sales sold
+  in the days, inclusive), `actual` (all `consume` movements in the days) and
+  `difference` (actual − theoretical), where either is above zero.
